1
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
The 4th film by Quentin Tarantino. Uncut, unrated, and shown in its entirety.

2
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Kill Bill: The Whole Bloody Affair is a action, crime
film directed by Quentin Tarantino.

3
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
A former assassin—known only as The Bride—wakes up from a coma after her former boss and lover,
Bill, shoots her in the head and steals her unborn child during her wedding rehearsal.

4
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
She soon embarks on a bloody quest for revenge, hunting down her ex-colleagues of
the Deadly Viper Assassination Squad before confronting Bill himself.

5
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Quentin Tarantino’s complete Kill Bill, a combination of Volumes 1 and 2, previously deleted scenes, alternate takes, a
full-color remaster of the Crazy 88 fight, a 7-minute anime sequence by Production I.G., and a built-in intermission.

6
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
The Bride / Beatrix Kiddo (Black Mamba) / Mommy, played by Uma Thurman.

7
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
O-Ren Ishii (Cottonmouth), played by Lucy Liu.

8
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,000
Vernita Green (Copperhead), played by Vivica A. Fox.

9
01:57:00,000 --> 01:57:06,000
Budd (Sidewinder), played by Michael Madsen.

10
02:10:00,000 --> 02:10:06,000
Elle Driver (California Mountain Snake), played by Daryl Hannah.

11
02:23:00,000 --> 02:23:06,000
Bill (Snake Charmer), played by David Carradine.

12
02:36:00,000 --> 02:36:06,000
Kill Bill: The Whole Bloody Affair is a 2006 American martial arts
film written and directed by Quentin Tarantino.

13
02:49:00,000 --> 02:49:06,000
It combines the films Kill Bill: Volume 1 (2003) and Kill Bill: Volume 2 (2004),
which were conceived and produced as a single film, but split in two.

14
03:02:00,000 --> 03:02:06,000
Uma Thurman stars as the Bride, who swears revenge on a group of
assassins after they try to kill her and her unborn child.

15
03:15:00,000 --> 03:15:06,000
Kill Bill: The Whole Bloody Affair premiered at the Cannes Film Festival in May
2006 and screened at Tarantino's New Beverly Cinema in 2011.

16
03:28:00,000 --> 03:28:06,000
Tarantino said he had waited until he owned the rights before giving the film a full release
and thought that asking audiences to come to his theater gave it more meaning.

17
03:41:00,000 --> 03:41:06,000
It was theatrically released in the United States by
Lionsgate on December 5, 2025, to critical acclaim.

18
03:54:00,000 --> 03:54:06,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, kung fu, revenge, aggressive, absurd.
